Box:
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\text{If }\Re\lambda(A)<0\text{ for all }\lambda\in\sigma(A)\setminus\{0\},\text{ and }0\notin\sigma(A)\text{ or }0\text{ is semisimple},\\
&\qquad\lim_{t\to\infty}e^{At}=P_0=V\operatorname{diag}(0,\ldots,0,1,\ldots,1)V^{-1},\\
&\text{where the }1\text{'s correspond to the }0\text{-eigenvalues (and }P_0=0\text{ if none). Otherwise the limit does not exist as a finite matrix.}
\end{aligned}
}
